{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470495-the-prestor-serums","id":1470495,"title":"The Prestor Serums","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-14T19:52:13-08:00","id":1470495,"title":"The Prestor Serums","content":"(This is adapted from something that appeared in the old adventure &quot;Alien Hunger.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Anonymous tips led FIRSTLIGHT to raid unregistered facilities under the Denver International Airport. These raids proved fruitful and allowed FIRSTLIGHT to destroy a lot of blank bodies and to confiscate property.<br /> Confiscated property included cars, guns and a wooden box containing some stoppered glass vials and a set of notes. The notes asserted the contents of the vials could change the nature of the blank bodies. On a lark, and suggestions from \u201cDr. Bierce,\u201d some operates tried some of the serum on a captured blank body.<br /> It worked. The subject transformed from an N-Type (Nosferatu Family) to something else and a different set of non-human abilities. The subject also developed an attractive physical appearance. In fact the non-human abilities displayed aligned most with T-Type blank bodies (Toreador Family). A second test transformed a subject blank body into a mortal who died.<br /> The tactical possibilities of the serums \u2013 named for a label found inside the lid of the box \u2013 are considerable. A target blank body might he handicapped by a forcible change to their subspecies, or neutralized by turning them into a human. The problem is FIRSTLIGHT has a limited supply of the serums and do not know how to make more. Dr. Bierce is assisting a team of high profile scientists on the issue. They conduct the research at Blacksite 24.<br /> <br /> The vials;<ul><li>3 empty tubes bearing labels reading \u201cSerum #1; Georges / L.\u201d, \u201cSerum #2; Neutral,\u201d and \u201cSerum #3; M. &amp; S. J., V. B.\u201d</li> <li>19 vials with a variety of letter combinations on the labels. Dr. Bierce and his staff believe there is a least one vial dedicated to each of the known subspecies of the blank bodies. These vials contain a dark red viscous material the team believes is blood altered in an unknown manner.</li> <li>Four vials containing a clear, thick, liquid. These bear the labels \u201cAnti-body Test #1\u201d through \u201cAnti-body Test #4.\u201d</li> <li>Two vials containing a white power. These bear labels reading \u201cResidue #1\u201d and \u201cResidue #2.\u201d</li> <li>Each vial could contain 120 ml below the stopper. Some have been partly used.</li> <li>A dosage is 30 ml.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Results and Effects<ul><li>A character taking a single dosage from Serum #1 will gain one generation to a maximum of 8th.</li> <li>Serum #2 has no effect.</li> <li>There is no effect for a character taking a dosage from a vial matching their clan.</li> <li>There is an effect for a character taking a dosage from a vial matching their clan. The player must roll a d10. On a 1-4 nothing happens. One a 5-8 the character\u2019s clan changes to that of the serum. On a 9 the character becomes a caitiff. On a 10 the character gains a discipline of the serum\u2019s clan. This does not change history as any characters remember, alter existing blood bonds, generation or blood potency.</li> <li>Anti-body serums #1 and #2 restore a vampire to humanity only for them to die. Anyone subject to these serums must roll humanity against a difficulty of 4. With 3 or more successes the character is alive and human but will die in less than a minute. This should give the player long enough for a brief speech.</li> <li>Anti-body serums #3 and #4 restore a vampire to humanity without dying. Anyone subject to these serums must roll humanity against a difficulty of 4. Every success means the loss of a point of blood potency. At zero blood potency the character has returned to humanity. The shock may kill them. They suffer an automatic wound for every hunger dice they have during the transformation.</li> <li>Subjects must drink the general serums.</li> <li>The anti-body serums need injection.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> [sidebar]<br /> Dr. Ambrose \u201cDr. Bierce\u201d Dexter Junior is an advisor to the Second Inquisition. He serves as a consultant for FIRSTLIGHT about work involving the section which holds the Prestor Serums. No one can remember who hired him or brought him no board. But that is not unusual for the S.I. which is bound by its own secrets. He taught at a small but prestigious university in East Texas before working with FIRSTLIGHT.<br /> His name appears in the \u00dcr-Codex though it does not go into details.<br /> [sidebar]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Google Dr. Ambrose Dexter </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 12-15-2021, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T06:26:00-08:00","id":1470525,"title":"","content":"I remember liking that adventure with Louis Pasteur. It looks like you came up with a good update for volume 5. I'd say that there should be a limit on how low the generation is affected. Going from 13 to 12 was sort of innocuous, Helena going from 4th to 3rd would be a little crazy. I'd set a generational limit to who could benefit from that one. Maybe all of them. Someone like Annabelle probably shouldn't find herself a 6th generation Gangrel.<br /> <br /> Actually as I type this I'm starting to remember, didn't they become vampires through the serum? Did the vials only work on vampires created by Pasteur? That would make sense. Maybe I'll reread it over the holidays, it's been decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T07:51:15-08:00","id":1470526,"title":"","content":"That is a good point about generations and Helena. I will make a note of it. On the other hand, someone turning her - or at least trying to do so - into a Nos would be interesting.<br /> I am hand waving the issue of who the serums can and cannot work on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T12:30:58-08:00","id":1470652,"title":"","content":"\u2022 Dr. Dexter\u2019s team believes the serums may be synthesized from the pineal gland. But it will take a lot of them. And taking a pineal gland will kill a person. So FIRSTLIGHT is collecting the bodies of executed prisoners and military personnel dead in accidents from across the Midwest. These bodies are sent to the University Park Medical Center in Gary, Indiana. Prince Maxwell of Gary knows the bodies are coming in large numbers but not why. He thinks it is something the Hecata are doing. He is going to put some pressure on them for operating in his city without putting his permission. They have no idea what he talking about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}